{{- /*
Pinned host-tool provisioning. Update version, URL, and checksum together.

Single-binary tools (rg/fd/fzf/lazygit/tree-sitter/rainfrog) land straight on PATH at
.local/bin/<tool> via `archive-file`. Neovim and Go are whole runtime trees, so
they are extracted with `archive` into .local/opt (exact = true drops old-version
files on upgrade) and exposed via .local/bin symlinks on Unix
(dot_local/bin/symlink_nvim.tmpl), or via PATH directly on Windows
(run_onchange_after_10-windows-path.ps1.tmpl; Windows symlinks need Developer
Mode/admin, so they aren't used there).

.local/bin is expected to already be on PATH on Unix; the Windows PATH
script adds the equivalent directories once.
*/ -}}

